# 2. REQUIRED TECHNOLOGY STACK

Use modern, stable and mutually compatible versions of the following technologies. Check the latest stable documentation and package compatibility before implementation. Avoid deprecated APIs and abandoned dependencies.

## Frontend
- React.js.
- TypeScript.
- Vite.
- Tailwind CSS.
- Modern CSS architecture.
- React Router.
- TanStack Query for server-state management.
- React Hook Form.
- Zod for client-side validation.
- Lucide React icons.
- Recharts for analytics and visual reporting.
- Framer Motion or an actively maintained compatible motion library.

## Backend
- Node.js.
- Express.js.
- TypeScript.
- RESTful API architecture.
- Zod request validation.
- Secure authentication and authorisation.
- Centralised error handling.
- Structured logging.
- Rate limiting.
- API documentation using OpenAPI/Swagger.

## Database
- MySQL 8 or a newer compatible stable release.
- Drizzle ORM.
- Drizzle Kit.
- Proper relational database design.
- Foreign-key constraints.
- Database migrations.
- Transaction management.
- Indexed queries.
- Soft deletion where appropriate.

## Security
- Argon2id password hashing.
- Secure HTTP-only cookies.
- CSRF protection where applicable.
- Role-based access control.
- Helmet security headers.
- Rate limiting.
- Input validation and sanitisation.
- Secure file upload validation.
- Audit logging.
- Session management.
- MFA support for administrative accounts.

## Infrastructure
- Environment-based configuration.
- Docker and Docker Compose.
- Separate development and production environments.
- Private file/object storage.
- Database backups.
- Deployment-ready configuration.
- Health-check endpoints.

Do not use Firebase or Supabase as substitutes for the requested Node.js and MySQL backend.

Do not replace Drizzle ORM with Prisma or Sequelize.

Do not use localStorage as the primary storage for authentication tokens or sensitive information.

