# 12. HUMANITARIAN PRIVACY AND SAFEGUARDING

This is one of the most important parts of the platform.

People using this platform may be affected by conflict, displacement, poverty, violence or other sensitive circumstances.

Protect their dignity and safety.

Implement:

### Consent Management
- Explicit consent before publishing stories.
- Separate consent for photographs and videos.
- Separate consent for public identification.
- Anonymous publication options.
- Consent withdrawal procedures.
- Consent records with timestamps.

### Privacy Protection
- Do not publish private telephone numbers.
- Do not publish residential addresses.
- Do not expose precise locations of vulnerable people.
- Do not expose confidential documents.
- Restrict access to sensitive information.
- Use private file storage.
- Use signed, expiring file-access links.
- Keep public and confidential case data separate.

### Child Safeguarding
- Special restrictions for children's information.
- Appropriate guardian consent.
- No public exposure of identifying information.
- No direct public contact functionality targeting children.
- Restrict sensitive child-related records to authorised reviewers.
- Provide a procedure to reject unsafe publication requests.

### Case Verification
- Separate submitted, under-review, verified, rejected and closed statuses.
- Require evidence appropriate to the type of case.
- Record who verified each case.
- Record verification timestamps.
- Maintain a complete decision history.

Never automatically classify a person as vulnerable or a case as genuine based solely on an AI-generated assessment.

Human review is mandatory.

